# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Lampose Stay Partner — environment
#
# Copy to `.env`. Expo inlines every EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable at BUILD time, so
# a change here needs the dev server restarted (and a rebuild for a release
# binary) — there is no runtime environment to read on a phone.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── The backend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED. This is the only place the app will look for a base URL.
#
# The API origin, WITHOUT a trailing slash and WITHOUT `/api`.
#
#   right   http://192.168.1.5:5001
#   right   https://api.lampose.com
#   wrong   http://192.168.1.5:5001/api      ← that is the web frontend's form
#
# Every path in services/api/endpoints.ts already starts `/api/v2/...`, the
# same way Backend/routes/index.js writes them, so a route can be read off one
# file and found in the other. A trailing `/api` is stripped defensively, but
# do not rely on it.
#
# UNLIKE THE USER APP, there is no development fallback. That app derives a
# host from wherever Metro served the bundle when this is unset; this one
# refuses to call anything at all.
#
# The reason is what this app is. It is the owner's console — it reads their
# bookings and it will move their money. A build that quietly falls back to
# somebody's laptop, or to a URL typed into a source file once, is a build
# that can be pointed at the wrong environment without anyone noticing until
# a payout lands in the wrong ledger. Requiring the variable makes the target
# of every build an explicit, reviewable fact.
#
# With it unset the app still starts and still renders. Every request fails
# immediately with `API_NOT_CONFIGURED`, the console prints what to set, and
# `useHealth().configured` is false — a diagnosable state rather than a blank
# screen that looks like a backend outage.
#
# On a physical device, `localhost` is the DEVICE. Use the LAN address of the
# machine running the backend. The Android emulator reaches its host on
# 10.0.2.2.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:5001


# ── Which API version ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not configurable, and deliberately so.
#
# This app is a v2 client on every route it has. v1 is the onboarding and
# admin surface: its writes create properties on a Lampose employee's behalf
# and need an administrator's grant. The version is written into each path in
# endpoints.ts rather than being a setting, so it cannot be repointed by an
# environment variable.
